#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:41
msgid "Main differences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:13
msgid "Maximum file size: 20 MB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:14
msgid "Works only with the HXL standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:15
msgid ""
"The table view after the error check is limited, and the user needs to "
"navigate through several tabs if the file has many lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:16
msgid "Does not include a publication feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:18
msgid "IATI Validator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:20
msgid ""
"Available at: "
"[https://validator.iatistandard.org/](https://validator.iatistandard.org/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:24
msgid "Works only with the IATI standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:25
msgid "Targets a specific sector, the international aid community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:26
msgid ""
"The tool offers five levels of qualification regarding data quality "
"(Success, Success with Advisories, Warning, Error, and Critical), rather "
"than a list of all errors and how to correct them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:28
msgid "CSV Lint.io"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:30
msgid "Available at: [https://csvlint.io/](https://csvlint.io/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:34
msgid ""
"Works only with CSV files, informing the user if the file “is readable” "
"or not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/introduction/similar-tools-and-differentiators.md:35
msgid "Agnostic tool; the schema can also be ingested."
msgstr ""

